                                "sense_id": "8eb66d8f-6260-3397-aef9-0606ff673327",
                                "text": "The Cauſe of this Diſeaſe, whether Sympathic from abroad, or Protopathic ingender’d in the Blood, is laid in a Salt, ſerous Humour lodged in the Glandules of the Skin, which have been deſcribed in our Introduction, raiſing up the Cuticle into ſmall Puſtules or Pimples, with white and ſhining Heads, which being rub’d in ſcratching, ouze out a clear Water and then dry up again with a Scab; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b6f81f5-357b-4299-b733-a90aa5898127",
                                "sense_id": "8eb66d8f-6260-3397-aef9-0606ff673327",
                                "text": "The sympathic system is peculiar to all insects, but in the several orders it takes a different form: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "475fba07-d4ae-409d-9c4f-22652d9acee0",
                                "sense_id": "8eb66d8f-6260-3397-aef9-0606ff673327",
                                "text": "The sympathic trunks run along each side of the aorta and the back of the abdomen into the hæmal canal; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
